\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces Moody's Aaa corporate bond yield and the Treasury yield, 1919--2025 (approximate annual averages). Panel~(a) shows the two yields, and panel~(b) shows the credit spread $s_t^{\text  {credit}} = y_t^{\text  {Aaa}} - y_t^{\text  {Tsy}}$. The Treasury yield is the long-term government bond yield before 1953 and the 10-year constant-maturity yield afterward. Shaded areas are recessions dated by the National Bureau of Economic Research (NBER).}}{182}{figure.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:aaa-treasury-spread}{{13.1}{182}{Moody's Aaa corporate bond yield and the Treasury yield, 1919--2025 (approximate annual averages). Panel~(a) shows the two yields, and panel~(b) shows the credit spread $s_t^{\text {credit}} = y_t^{\text {Aaa}} - y_t^{\text {Tsy}}$. The Treasury yield is the long-term government bond yield before 1953 and the 10-year constant-maturity yield afterward. Shaded areas are recessions dated by the National Bureau of Economic Research (NBER)}{figure.caption.48}{}}
